# Authoritative floating-point dot-product verification target

Use the abstract relative-error Model and binary reduction Tree supplied in the
candidate project. Prove, for every model and every tree of pairs of real
numbers, that if `(tree.depth + 1) * model.u < 1`, rounding each componentwise
product and then reducing the rounded products with rounded tree addition is the
exact sum of leafwise perturbations of the exact products.

The perturbation bound must be `gamma (tree.depth + 1) model.u`: one rounding
error comes from each multiplication and at most `tree.depth` errors come from
the additions on a leaf-to-root path. The theorem must relate the result to
`exactProductTree tree`, account for both multiplication and addition rounding,
and may not assume its conclusion or restrict the model to exact arithmetic.

The intended target has the mathematical content of
`roundedDotProduct_exists_perturbation`; declaration names and proof order are
not requirements.
{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "target-completeness",
      "description": "Prove the full universally quantified dot-product backward-error theorem."
    },
    {
      "id": "exact-product-linkage",
      "description": "Relate perturbations to exact componentwise products x_i*y_i."
    },
    {
      "id": "multiplication-rounding",
      "description": "Account for one rounded multiplication per leaf."
    },
    {
      "id": "addition-reduction",
      "description": "Account for every rounded tree addition in the reduction."
    },
    {
      "id": "accumulated-bound",
      "description": "Establish the gamma(depth+1,u) componentwise perturbation bound."
    },
    {
      "id": "assumption-integrity",
      "description": "Use only the stated model and smallness assumptions without assuming or restricting the conclusion."
    }
  ],
  "defect_categories": [
    {
      "id": "missing-final-theorem",
      "description": "The target proposition is not proved."
    },
    {
      "id": "missing-exact-product-link",
      "description": "The proof is relative to rounded products rather than exact x_i*y_i products."
    },
    {
      "id": "multiplication-rounding-omitted",
      "description": "The multiplication error is omitted from the analysis."
    },
    {
      "id": "addition-rounding-omitted",
      "description": "The reduction-addition errors are omitted from the analysis."
    },
    {
      "id": "wrong-error-count",
      "description": "The accumulated bound uses the wrong number of rounding errors."
    },
    {
      "id": "strengthened-assumption",
      "description": "The theorem adds an assumption not present in the requested result."
    },
    {
      "id": "conclusion-assumed",
      "description": "The desired conclusion or an equivalent statement is assumed."
    },
    {
      "id": "weakened-quantification",
      "description": "The theorem covers fewer models or trees than requested."
    }
  ]
}
